            "imageUrl": "https://f.civitatis.com/paises-bajos/amsterdam/entrada-ripley-believe-it-not.jpg",
            "description": "Prepare to immerse yourself in a world of astounding optical illusions and an impressive 7-meter (23-foot) robot at the ultimate illusion museum located in Amsterdam.Ticket for the Illusion Museum in AmsterdamEmbark on an adventure through the captivating realm of this illusion museum in Amsterdam. With your entry ticket, you will unlock access to 19 uniquely themed galleries, showcasing extraordinary natural, scientific, artistic, and human marvels from across the globe. Spanning over 5 floors filled with fun, the experience is sure to challenge your perceptions!Delve into intriguing narratives that cover topics from the achievements of ancient societies to modern artistic creations. Snap a picture beside the statue of the tallest individual in modern history, towering at 2.72 meters (8 feet 11 inches), traverse the only space tunnel in the Netherlands, and engage with astonishing optical illusions and much more!Lounge Area at the MuseumYour ticket also grants you access to the lounge area, where you can unwind while enjoying breathtaking panoramic views of Dam Square—a key landmark in Europe. This museum truly has an abundance to offer!Visiting HoursThe illusion museum welcomes visitors every day of the year from 11 am to 7 pm, with the final entry at 6 pm. Notably, during the period from December 3 to 19, the last entry is at 4 pm.On December 24th, 25th, and 31st, the museum operates from 10 am to 5 pm; on December 26th, it remains open from 10 am to 10 pm; and on January 1st, from 12 pm to 8 pm. As a reminder, the last entry always occurs one hour before the museum closes.",
